IMPORT prelude

-- Land Titles Act 1993 (Singapore) -- Part 17, the civil rights and remedies:
-- the assurance fund and the action for damages against it.
--
-- ss 151 to 159, with s 46 (the indefeasibility provision that does the barring)
-- and s 51A(4) (the electronic-lodgment provision that narrows what counts as a
-- mistake of the Registrar).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 23 September 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/LTA1993.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate.
--
-- SCOPE. The Act is about 325,000 characters. This encodes one Part of nineteen,
-- plus the two sections outside it that Part 17 cannot be read without. Nothing
-- here touches registration, caveats, easements, leases, mortgages, strata, or
-- the court's rectification power in s 160.

§ `Land Titles Act 1993 -- Part 17, the assurance fund`

§§ `46 -- what the register does to the dispossessed owner`

-- s 46(1): "Despite -- (a) the existence in any other person of any estate or
-- interest ... which but for this Act might be held to be paramount ...; and
-- (b) any failure to observe the procedural requirements of this Act, any person
-- who becomes the proprietor of registered land, WHETHER OR NOT THAT PERSON
-- DEALT WITH A PROPRIETOR, AND DESPITE ANY LACK OF GOOD FAITH ON THE PART OF THE
-- PERSON THROUGH WHOM THAT PERSON CLAIMS, holds that land free from all
-- encumbrances, liens, estates and interests except such as may be registered or
-- notified in the land-register", subject to nine exceptions in (c) to (i).
--
-- s 46(2): "Nothing in this section shall be held to prejudice the rights and
-- remedies of any person --
--   (a) to have the registered title of a proprietor defeated on the ground of
--       FRAUD OR FORGERY TO WHICH THAT PROPRIETOR OR THAT PROPRIETOR'S AGENT WAS
--       A PARTY or in which that proprietor or that proprietor's agent colluded;
--   (b) to enforce against a proprietor any contract to which that proprietor was
--       a party;
--   (c) to enforce against a proprietor who is a trustee the provisions of the
--       trust;
--   (d) to recover from a proprietor land acquired by him or her from a person
--       under a legal disability which was known to the proprietor at the time of
--       dealing; or
--   (e) to recover from a proprietor land which has been UNLAWFULLY ACQUIRED by
--       him or her in purported exercise of a statutory power or authority."
--
-- s 46(3): "Nothing in this section confers on a proprietor claiming OTHERWISE
-- THAN AS A PURCHASER any better title than was held by the proprietor's
-- immediate predecessor."
--
-- The shape of it: a purchaser is protected against their predecessor's fraud
-- and not against their own. So where a forger registers and sells on, the
-- innocent buyer keeps the land and the dispossessed owner's only proprietary
-- remedy is against the forger.
DECLARE Proprietor HAS
    `became the proprietor of registered land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a party to, or colluded in, the fraud or forgery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor's agent was a party to or colluded in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a predecessor in title acted in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims as a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired the land from a person under a known legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawfully acquired the land in purported exercise of a statutory power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a party to the contract sought to be enforced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a trustee of the land` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the proprietor` IS A Proprietor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` IF
        `the proprietor`'s `was a party to, or colluded in, the fraud or forgery`
    OR  `the proprietor`'s `the proprietor's agent was a party to or colluded in it`
    OR  `the proprietor`'s `was a party to the contract sought to be enforced`
    OR  `the proprietor`'s `is a trustee of the land`
    OR  `the proprietor`'s `acquired the land from a person under a known legal disability`
    OR  `the proprietor`'s `unlawfully acquired the land in purported exercise of a statutory power`

-- s 46(3): a volunteer -- a donee, a beneficiary under a will, anyone claiming
-- otherwise than as a purchaser -- takes no better title than their predecessor
-- had. So the forger's gift to a relative is reachable where the forger's sale to
-- a buyer is not.
GIVEN `the proprietor` IS A Proprietor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 46(3) leaves this proprietor exposed to the predecessor's defect` IF
        NOT `the proprietor`'s `claims as a purchaser`
    AND `the proprietor`'s `a predecessor in title acted in bad faith`

GIVEN `the proprietor` IS A Proprietor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` IF
        `the proprietor`'s `became the proprietor of registered land`
    AND NOT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `the proprietor`
    AND NOT `section 46(3) leaves this proprietor exposed to the predecessor's defect` `the proprietor`

§§ `157(1) -- and the same thing said again`

-- s 157(1): "DESPITE ANYTHING IN THIS ACT, no purchaser who has become a
-- proprietor may be subject to action for the recovery of land or of money ON
-- THE PLEA THAT THE PURCHASER'S VENDOR, OR ANY PREDECESSOR IN TITLE, MAY HAVE
-- ACTED IN BAD FAITH."
--
-- This covers the same ground as the closing words of s 46(1) and adds "or of
-- money", so the dispossessed owner cannot pursue the innocent purchaser for the
-- value either. The two provisions together are what leave the owner with the
-- fund and the forger and nothing else.
--
-- s 157(2): neither the Authority, the Registrar, nor anyone acting under their
-- authority is PERSONALLY liable for anything "in good faith done or omitted to
-- be done in the administration of this Act". So the claim lies against the fund
-- and not against the official, and the official's good faith is no answer to
-- the fund -- s 155 asks about omission, mistake or misfeasance, not about bad
-- faith.
GIVEN `the proprietor` IS A Proprietor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 157(1) bars an action against this proprietor for the land or the money` IF
        `the proprietor`'s `claims as a purchaser`
    AND `the proprietor`'s `became the proprietor of registered land`
    AND NOT `the proprietor`'s `was a party to, or colluded in, the fraud or forgery`
    AND NOT `the proprietor`'s `the proprietor's agent was a party to or colluded in it`

GIVEN `the Registrar or an officer acted in good faith in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 157(2) protects the official personally` IF
    `the Registrar or an officer acted in good faith in the administration of this Act`

-- s 155 asks whether there was an omission, mistake or misfeasance. It does not
-- ask whether the Registrar was at fault in any moral sense, and s 157(2) does
-- not touch the fund.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar's good faith is an answer to a claim against the fund` IF
    FALSE

§§ `154 -- the proprietary actions that survive`

-- s 154(1): "No action of ejectment or other action for the recovery of
-- registered land lies or may be sustained against the proprietor thereof EXCEPT
-- in the case of --
--   (a) a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default;
--   (b) a chargee against a chargor in default;
--   (c) a lessor against a lessee in default;
--   (d) A PERSON DEPRIVED OF LAND BY FRAUD AGAINST THE PERSON WHO HAS BECOME
--       REGISTERED AS PROPRIETOR OF THE LAND BY FRAUD, OR AGAINST ANY PERSON
--       CLAIMING THROUGH THAT PROPRIETOR OTHERWISE THAN AS A PURCHASER; or
--   (e) a re-entry or forfeiture upon breach of a covenant or condition contained
--       or implied in a State title."
--
-- s 154(3): in an action based on fraudulent deprivation "the court may make an
-- order for payment of DAMAGES either IN ADDITION TO OR IN SUBSTITUTION FOR an
-- order for the recovery of land."
-- s 154(4): the court is to have regard to improvements made since the
--   deprivation and to the conduct of the parties, and "may, if it sees fit, put
--   the successful party on terms of PAYING COMPENSATION."
-- s 154(5): "any UNLAWFUL ACQUISITION of land, whether by a person purporting to
--   act under statutory authority or otherwise, is DEEMED TO BE FRAUDULENT."
--
-- s 154(5) is wide. It brings an acquisition under a statutory power that turned
-- out to be invalid inside limb (d) without anyone having to prove dishonesty.
DECLARE RecoveryAction HAS
    `a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a chargee against a chargor in default` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lessor against a lessee in default` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant was deprived of land by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land was unlawfully acquired, whether or not under purported statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant became registered as proprietor by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant claims through that proprietor otherwise than as a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a re-entry or forfeiture on breach of a State title covenant` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 154(5) deems the unlawful acquisition fraudulent, so it supplies both halves
-- of limb (d) where the acquirer is the registered proprietor.
GIVEN `the action` IS A RecoveryAction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there was a deprivation by fraud for the purposes of section 154` IF
        `the action`'s `the claimant was deprived of land by fraud`
    OR  `the action`'s `the land was unlawfully acquired, whether or not under purported statutory authority`

GIVEN `the action` IS A RecoveryAction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 154(1)(d) permits the action` IF
        `there was a deprivation by fraud for the purposes of section 154` `the action`
    AND (    `the action`'s `the defendant became registered as proprietor by fraud`
         OR  `the action`'s `the defendant claims through that proprietor otherwise than as a purchaser`)

GIVEN `the action` IS A RecoveryAction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` IF
        `the action`'s `a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default`
    OR  `the action`'s `a chargee against a chargor in default`
    OR  `the action`'s `a lessor against a lessee in default`
    OR  `section 154(1)(d) permits the action` `the action`
    OR  `the action`'s `a re-entry or forfeiture on breach of a State title covenant`

§§ `51A(4) -- the Registrar stops having to look`

-- s 51A(4): where an instrument is lodged in electronic form --
--   "(a) it is the duty of the person who certifies the correctness of the
--        instrument under section 59 to ensure that all particulars entered
--        therein are complete and accurate; and
--    (b) THE REGISTRAR NEED NOT BE CONCERNED TO INQUIRE INTO THE COMPLETENESS OR
--        ACCURACY of the particulars as entered in the instrument and MUST, on
--        acceptance of the instrument so lodged, REGISTER THE INSTRUMENT IN
--        ACCORDANCE WITH THOSE PARTICULARS."
--
-- s 155(1) requires the deprivation or loss to be "through any omission, mistake
-- or misfeasance of the Registrar, or any member of the Registrar's staff". s 51A
-- removes the duty of inquiry on an electronic lodgment and makes registration
-- mandatory on the particulars given. Where the Registrar had no duty to look and
-- was obliged to register what was lodged, it is hard to see what the omission or
-- mistake is.
--
-- So the modernisation of lodgment narrowed the assurance fund without amending
-- Part 17. The encoding records the point rather than deciding it: a function
-- that reports whether the Registrar bore a duty of inquiry, and a separate one
-- for whether a mistake is established.
DECLARE RegistrarsConduct HAS
    `the instrument was lodged in electronic form under section 51A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar omitted something, made a mistake, or committed a misfeasance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what went wrong was an inaccuracy in the particulars as lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it occurred in bringing the land under this Act or in registering an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A RegistrarsConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar bore a duty to inquire into the accuracy of the particulars` IF
    NOT `the conduct`'s `the instrument was lodged in electronic form under section 51A`

-- Where the only thing that went wrong was an inaccuracy in the particulars of
-- an electronically lodged instrument, s 51A(4) put the duty on the certifier
-- and took it off the Registrar.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A RegistrarsConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` IF
        `the conduct`'s `it occurred in bringing the land under this Act or in registering an instrument`
    AND `the conduct`'s `the Registrar omitted something, made a mistake, or committed a misfeasance`
    AND (    NOT `the conduct`'s `what went wrong was an inaccuracy in the particulars as lodged`
         OR  `the Registrar bore a duty to inquire into the accuracy of the particulars` `the conduct`)

§§ `155 -- the action against the assurance fund`

-- s 155(1): "SUBJECT TO SUBSECTION (3), any person who is deprived of land or
-- sustains loss or damage THROUGH ANY OMISSION, MISTAKE OR MISFEASANCE OF THE
-- REGISTRAR, or any member of the Registrar's staff, in the bringing of the land
-- under the provisions of this Act or in the registration of any instrument, AND
-- WHO IS BARRED BY THIS ACT FROM BRINGING ANY ACTION FOR THE RECOVERY of land,
-- proceeds of the sale of land, moneys secured by a registered mortgage or
-- interests protected by a caveat notified on a folio, may bring an action for
-- the recovery of damages against the assurance fund."
--
-- Three elements, and the first is the one a layperson will not expect.
--
--   (1) THE REGISTRAR MUST HAVE GOT SOMETHING WRONG. The fund does not insure the
--       register's effect; it insures the Registrar's conduct. A clean forgery
--       that the Registrar registered correctly on its face gives no claim at
--       all, however complete the owner's loss.
--   (2) The claimant must be BARRED BY THIS ACT from an action for the recovery
--       of land, proceeds of sale, mortgage moneys or caveated interests.
--   (3) None of the s 155(3) exclusions applies.
--
-- s 155(4): "For the purposes of this section, any person who MAY BRING an action
-- for the recovery of land, proceeds of sale of land or moneys secured by a
-- registered mortgage or charge, or interests protected by a caveat notified on
-- a folio IS DEEMED NOT TO HAVE BEEN DEPRIVED of the land or suffered any loss or
-- damage, as the case may be."
--
-- s 155(4) is stronger than element (2). It does not merely withhold the fund
-- claim from a person with another remedy; it deems them to have suffered NO LOSS
-- AT ALL. So the owner who can sue the absconded forger for the proceeds of sale
-- has, for the purposes of s 155, lost nothing.
--
-- s 155(2): the court "is to take into consideration the fact that the
-- CLAIMANT'S OWN NEGLECT, DEFAULT OR INCAUTION may have caused or contributed to
-- the deprivation, loss or damage, and in any such case MAY WITHHOLD OR ABATE
-- damages or compensation accordingly." Contributory fault can defeat the claim
-- entirely, not merely reduce it.
--
-- s 155(3): "NO COMPENSATION IS TO BE PAID out of the assurance fund UNDER ANY
-- CIRCUMSTANCES for any loss, damage or deprivation occasioned by --
--   (a) the issue of a QUALIFIED FOLIO for the land brought under the provisions
--       of this Act;
--   (b) any INCORRECT DESCRIPTION OF THE PARCELS, THE BOUNDARIES OR DIMENSIONS
--       (INCLUDING AREA) of any land provided by the Chief Surveyor or any
--       incorrect particulars of the alienation of the land forwarded by the
--       Collector to the Registrar; or
--   (c) any incorrect description or lack of description of the parcels or
--       dimensions (including area) of any land or a strata lot WHERE NO SURVEY
--       HAS BEEN CARRIED OUT."
--
-- Limbs (b) and (c) exclude the commonest practical error in a land register:
-- getting the boundaries or the area wrong. "Under any circumstances", so no
-- degree of fault in the Registrar brings it back.
--
-- s 151(5): and the fund "is NOT LIABLE to compensate any person suffering loss,
-- damage or deprivation occasioned by the BREACH BY A PROPRIETOR OF ANY TRUST."
DECLARE WhatWentWrong IS ONE OF
    `the issue of a qualified folio`
    `an incorrect description of the parcels, boundaries or dimensions from the Chief Surveyor`
    `incorrect particulars of the alienation of the land from the Collector`
    `an incorrect or absent description of parcels or dimensions where no survey was carried out`
    `a breach by a proprietor of a trust`
    `something else`

GIVEN `what went wrong` IS A WhatWentWrong
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 155(3) excludes compensation` IF
    CONSIDER `what went wrong`
    WHEN `the issue of a qualified folio` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an incorrect description of the parcels, boundaries or dimensions from the Chief Surveyor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `incorrect particulars of the alienation of the land from the Collector` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an incorrect or absent description of parcels or dimensions where no survey was carried out` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `what went wrong` IS A WhatWentWrong
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 151(5) excludes compensation` IF
    CONSIDER `what went wrong`
    WHEN `a breach by a proprietor of a trust` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE FundClaim HAS
    `the Registrar's conduct` IS A RegistrarsConduct
    `what went wrong` IS A WhatWentWrong
    `the claimant was deprived of land or sustained loss or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant may bring an action for the recovery of the land, the proceeds of sale, mortgage moneys or a caveated interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's own neglect, default or incaution contributed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has decided to withhold compensation altogether for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` IS A NUMBER
    `an earlier action for the same cause was discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since that discontinuance` IS A NUMBER
    `notice of the claim was served on the Registrar at least 14 days before commencement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 155(4): the deeming.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 155(4) deems the claimant to have suffered no loss` IF
    `the claim`'s `the claimant may bring an action for the recovery of the land, the proceeds of sale, mortgage moneys or a caveated interest`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant is barred from an action for recovery as section 155(1) requires` IF
    NOT `the claim`'s `the claimant may bring an action for the recovery of the land, the proceeds of sale, mortgage moneys or a caveated interest`

§§ `158 -- the limitation period, and the one event that extends it`

-- s 158(1): "No action under section 155 shall lie unless such action is
-- commenced WITHIN 12 YEARS FROM THE DATE ON WHICH THE DEPRIVATION OCCURRED OR
-- THE LOSS OR DAMAGE WAS SUSTAINED."
--
-- From the deprivation, not from discovery. A register error can sit undetected
-- for a generation, and the clock runs from the error.
--
-- s 158(2): "Where an action for deprivation, loss or damage has been commenced
-- against ANY PERSON within the period of 12 years ..., an action against the
-- assurance fund FOR THE SAME CAUSE may be commenced WITHIN ONE YEAR AFTER THE
-- DISCONTINUANCE OF THE FORMER ACTION, even though the period of 12 years may
-- have expired."
--
-- THE EXTENSION IS FOR DISCONTINUANCE AND NOTHING ELSE. The claimant whose
-- action against the forger is dismissed, or who fights it to judgment and
-- loses, or whose defendant is wound up with nothing in it, gets no extra year.
-- Read with s 155(4), which forces the claimant to exhaust that action before
-- the fund claim exists at all, the structure obliges the claimant to spend the
-- 12 years on a remedy whose failure in any manner other than discontinuance
-- leaves them with nothing.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is within the twelve years in section 158(1)` IF
    `the claim`'s `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 158(2) extends the time` IF
        `the claim`'s `an earlier action for the same cause was discontinued`
    AND `the claim`'s `years since that discontinuance` AT MOST 1

GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is in time` IF
        `the claim is within the twelve years in section 158(1)` `the claim`
    OR  `section 158(2) extends the time` `the claim`

§§ `155 and 156 together -- whether the claim lies`

-- s 156(1): a claimant "must, NOT LESS THAN 14 DAYS before the commencement of
-- the action, serve notice of the person's claim on the Registrar AS NOMINAL
-- DEFENDANT, stating the grounds on which the person's claim is made and the
-- amount claimed."
GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action against the assurance fund lies` IF
        `the claim`'s `the claimant was deprived of land or sustained loss or damage`
    AND `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` (`the claim`'s `the Registrar's conduct`)
    AND `the claimant is barred from an action for recovery as section 155(1) requires` `the claim`
    AND NOT `section 155(4) deems the claimant to have suffered no loss` `the claim`
    AND NOT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` (`the claim`'s `what went wrong`)
    AND NOT `section 151(5) excludes compensation` (`the claim`'s `what went wrong`)
    AND `the claim is in time` `the claim`
    AND `the claim`'s `notice of the claim was served on the Registrar at least 14 days before commencement`

-- s 155(2): and even where the action lies, the court may withhold compensation
-- altogether for the claimant's own neglect.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant recovers something from the fund` IF
        `an action against the assurance fund lies` `the claim`
    AND NOT `the claim`'s `the court has decided to withhold compensation altogether for that reason`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A FundClaim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may withhold or abate the compensation` IF
    `the claim`'s `the claimant's own neglect, default or incaution contributed`

§§ `155(6) and (7) -- the Registrar's offer ends the liability fight`

-- s 155(6): "On receipt of a notice, the Registrar is entitled to appear in any
-- such action and MAY OFFER TO COMPENSATE any party to the action out of the
-- assurance fund."
-- s 155(7): "On any such offer being made, FURTHER ACTION IS LIMITED TO
-- DETERMINATION OF THE COMPENSATION TO BE PAID."
--
-- So an offer -- not an acceptance, an offer -- converts the proceedings into an
-- assessment of quantum. Nothing in the subsection requires the claimant to
-- accept it or the amount to be adequate; the consequence attaches to the making
-- of the offer. The claimant who wanted a finding about the Registrar's conduct,
-- or who was pursuing some other relief in the same action, loses that.
GIVEN `the Registrar has offered to compensate out of the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `further action is limited to determining the compensation` IF
    `the Registrar has offered to compensate out of the fund`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant must accept the offer for section 155(7) to bite` IF
    FALSE

§§ `156(2) to (5) -- the costs rule, and the only safe outcome`

-- s 156(2): "The Registrar MAY TENDER in settlement of the claim the amount
-- claimed or any lesser amount, and if the claimant REJECTS that tender and
-- FAILS LATER TO RECOVER DAMAGES EXCEEDING THE AMOUNT TENDERED BY 20% OF THAT
-- AMOUNT, the claimant must pay, IN ADDITION TO THE CLAIMANT'S OWN COSTS, the
-- costs of the Registrar in defending the action."
--
-- Read it carefully. The claimant must beat the tender by MORE THAN A FIFTH, not
-- merely beat it. A claimant who rejects $100,000 and recovers $115,000 has won
-- the action and pays both sides' costs.
--
-- s 156(3): where "the claimant recovers FINAL JUDGMENT against the Registrar",
-- the damages and (except as provided in subsection (2)) the costs are paid to
-- the claimant and charged to the fund.
-- s 156(4): "IN ALL OTHER CASES, the Registrar's costs are payable by the
--   claimant."
--
-- So the claimant bears the Registrar's costs in every case except a final
-- judgment that also beats the tender by more than 20%. Settling bears them.
-- Winning by a margin of a fifth bears them.
--
-- s 156(5): "Despite anything to the contrary in section 155, any person deprived
-- of land to a value of NOT MORE THAN $1,000, or sustaining loss or damage of not
-- more than that amount, MAY CLAIM AGAINST THE ASSURANCE FUND IN THE FIRST
-- INSTANCE and the Registrar may settle or compound the claim."
--
-- "Despite anything to the contrary in section 155" -- so for a claim of $1,000
-- or less the s 155(4) deeming and the requirement of being barred from a
-- recovery action fall away, and the claimant goes straight to the fund. It is a
-- real simplification and it applies to a figure that buys very little land.
-- s 151(2) matches it: the Registrar may authorise payment of a claim "not
-- exceeding $1,000" alone, and anything above needs the Minister in writing or a
-- court.
DECLARE Tender HAS
    `the Registrar tendered an amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount tendered, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant rejected the tender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the damages recovered, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the claimant recovered final judgment against the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the figure the claimant must exceed under section 156(2)` IS
    `the tender`'s `the amount tendered, in dollars`
        PLUS (`the tender`'s `the amount tendered, in dollars` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100)

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant beat the tender by enough` IF
    `the tender`'s `the damages recovered, in dollars`
        GREATER THAN `the figure the claimant must exceed under section 156(2)` `the tender`

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 156(2) makes the claimant pay the Registrar's costs` IF
        `the tender`'s `the Registrar tendered an amount`
    AND `the tender`'s `the claimant rejected the tender`
    AND NOT `the claimant beat the tender by enough` `the tender`

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund bears the claimant's costs` IF
        `the tender`'s `the claimant recovered final judgment against the Registrar`
    AND NOT `section 156(2) makes the claimant pay the Registrar's costs` `the tender`

GIVEN `the tender` IS A Tender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` IF
    NOT `the fund bears the claimant's costs` `the tender`

`the ceiling on what the Registrar may authorise alone` MEANS 1000

GIVEN `the value of the deprivation or loss, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 156(5) lets the claimant go straight to the fund` IF
    `the value of the deprivation or loss, in dollars` AT MOST `the ceiling on what the Registrar may authorise alone`

GIVEN `the amount of the claim, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may authorise payment without the Minister or the court` IF
    `the amount of the claim, in dollars` AT MOST `the ceiling on what the Registrar may authorise alone`

§§ `159 -- the correction power, and the second route to the fund`

-- s 159(1): "The Registrar MAY, upon such evidence as appears to him or her
-- sufficient, CORRECT ERRORS AND OMISSIONS in the land-register."
-- s 159(2): without limiting that, the Registrar may of his or her own motion or
--   at the aggrieved proprietor's request correct a misspelt name, land already
--   in a prior folio, "or the WRONG DESCRIPTION OF PARCELS OR OF THE BOUNDARIES
--   OR DIMENSIONS (INCLUDING THE AREA) of the land", any erroneous entry or
--   endorsement, any erroneous omission, or cancel and re-create the folio.
-- s 159(4): in correcting, the Registrar "must have regard to any improvements to
--   the land which may have been made since the occurrence of the error and,
--   WHERE 2 OR MORE TITLES ARE INVOLVED, HE OR SHE MAY CORRECT THAT FOLIO, ENTRY
--   OR ENDORSEMENT WHICH IN HIS OR HER OPINION INVOLVES THE LEAST LOSS TO THE
--   ASSURANCE FUND."
-- s 159(5): "Any person who, HAVING DEALT ON THE FAITH OF AN ERRONEOUS
--   REGISTRATION, has suffered loss or damage BY THE EXERCISE OF THE POWER
--   CONFERRED ON THE REGISTRAR BY THIS SECTION is, SUBJECT TO SECTION 158,
--   entitled to be compensated from the assurance fund for the land of which the
--   person has been deprived AND FOR ANY IMPROVEMENT made thereon by the person
--   or by any predecessor in title, and may bring an action for the recovery of
--   such compensation."
--
-- TWO THINGS.
--
-- First, s 159(5) is a SECOND and INDEPENDENT route to the fund, and it is far
-- easier than s 155. It asks only that the claimant dealt on the faith of an
-- erroneous registration and lost by the correction. It does not require an
-- omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar; it does not require the
-- claimant to be barred from an action for recovery; and the s 155(4) deeming
-- does not apply to it. It is subject only to the s 158 limitation period. It is
-- also narrower in measure -- the land and the improvements, where s 155 speaks
-- of damages generally.
--
-- Second, the s 155(3)(b) and (c) exclusions do not qualify it. So the boundary
-- or area error, which s 155(3) excludes from compensation "under any
-- circumstances", becomes compensable under s 159(5) once the Registrar
-- exercises the s 159 power to correct it. The route to compensation for a
-- mis-described boundary runs through the Registrar choosing to correct the
-- register, and not otherwise.
--
-- And s 159(4) decides which of two innocent proprietors bears the loss by
-- reference to the fund's exposure rather than to their positions.
DECLARE Correction HAS
    `the Registrar has exercised the power to correct the land-register` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant dealt on the faith of the erroneous registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant suffered loss or damage by the correction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` IS A NUMBER
    `two or more titles are involved` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the correction` IS A Correction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is within the twelve years, for a section 159(5) claim` IF
    `the correction`'s `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `the correction` IS A Correction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is payable under section 159(5)` IF
        `the correction`'s `the Registrar has exercised the power to correct the land-register`
    AND `the correction`'s `the claimant dealt on the faith of the erroneous registration`
    AND `the correction`'s `the claimant suffered loss or damage by the correction`
    AND `the claim is within the twelve years, for a section 159(5) claim` `the correction`

-- The things s 159(5) does not ask for, stated so they can be asserted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 159(5) requires an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 159(5) requires the claimant to be barred from an action for recovery` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 155(3) exclusions apply to a section 159(5) claim` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the correction` IS A Correction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar chooses between the titles by what it costs the fund` IF
        `the correction`'s `two or more titles are involved`
    AND `the correction`'s `the Registrar has exercised the power to correct the land-register`

§§ `152 and 153 -- the two routes that the fund pays for either way`

-- s 152: where the Registrar refuses to register, or makes a requisition and
-- will not withdraw it, the applicant may require written grounds and "SUMMON
-- THE REGISTRAR TO APPEAR BEFORE THE COURT to substantiate and uphold the
-- grounds of his or her refusal". s 152(2) requires at least 6 clear days'
-- service. s 152(4): on any such summons the court may make such order as to
-- costs as it thinks just, "and any costs or expenses TO BE PAID BY THE REGISTRAR
-- are to be PAID OUT OF THE ASSURANCE FUND."
--
-- s 153: the Registrar may state a case for the court's opinion, and the court
-- may certify that a question of public importance is involved and that the
-- costs "are to be PAID OUT OF THE ASSURANCE FUND."
--
-- Both routes charge the fund. s 151(1) constitutes the fund out of a prescribed
-- proportion of the Registrar's fees "from which are to be paid -- (a) any sum
-- necessary to compensate claimants under section 155; and (b) ANY OTHER
-- DISBURSEMENTS that are directed or authorised to be paid, or expressed to be
-- recoverable, from that fund." So compensation under s 155 competes with the
-- costs of these proceedings for the same money -- although s 151(4) makes any
-- deficiency "charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund", so the
-- competition is about the fund's accounts rather than about whether a claimant
-- is paid.
GIVEN `the Registrar refused to comply with the application or withdraw the requisition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the summons was served at least 6 clear days before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may summon the Registrar under section 152` IF
        `the Registrar refused to comply with the application or withdraw the requisition`
    AND `the summons was served at least 6 clear days before the hearing`

GIVEN `the court ordered the Registrar to pay costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assurance fund bears those costs` IF
    `the court ordered the Registrar to pay costs`

-- s 151(4): the fund running dry is not the claimant's problem.
GIVEN `the amount to the credit of the assurance fund is inadequate to meet the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deficiency is charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund` IF
    `the amount to the credit of the assurance fund is inadequate to meet the claim`
